<title>USA: USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</title>
<headline>USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hide and offal value from a typical slaughter steer for today was estimated at 9.66 per cwt live, up $0.09 when compared to Wednesday's value. - USDA</p>
<p>FOB CENTRAL U.S., TODAY'S CALCULATIONS FOR BY-PRODUCT VALUE</p>
<p>(STEER) -			  Lbs    Price  Change    Value</p>
<p>Steer hide, butt brand	 5.38   85.00   -0.50    5.86</p>
<p>Tallow, edible		   1.20   24.75    0.50    0.30</p>
<p>Tallow, packer bleachable    4.50   23.25    2.50    1.05</p>
<p>Tongues, Swiss #1 Wht 0-3%   0.26  200.00    -	 0.52</p>
<p>Cheek meat, trmd		 0.32   68.00    -	 0.22</p>
<p>Head meat			  0.13   44.50    -	 0.06</p>
<p>Oxtail, selected		 0.16  131.00    -	 0.21</p>
<p>Hearts, reg, bone out	  0.38   23.50   -0.50    0.09</p>
<p>Lips, unscalded		  0.11   72.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Livers, slcted, gall off     0.96   35.00    -	 0.34</p>
<p>Tripe, scalded edible	  0.65   23.00    -	 0.15</p>
<p>Tripe, honeycomb bleached    0.15   50.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Lungs, inedible		  0.47    4.60    -	 0.02</p>
<p>Melts				0.14    6.25    -	 0.01</p>
<p>Meat bone ml, 50% blk/ton    3.70  265.00   -1.00    0.49</p>
<p>Blood meal, 85% blk/ton	0.60  585.00    -	 0.18</p>
<p>TOTAL :			   19.11			  9.66</p>
<p>The average value of hide and offal for the four days ending Thursday, January 9, 1997 was estimated at 9.64 per cwt, down -0.02 from last week and up 1.44 from last year.</p>
